  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social Care and Dementia Support to Jewish Communities 2025-26</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Jewish Relief has been working in Belarus since the 1990s, mainly in partnership with Hesed Rakhamim, which supports over 2,000 older Jewish people in Minsk who require medical and social support. This project proposes a continuation of support provided by the UK Embassy in 2024-25, allowing Hesed to build on existing best practice and continue supporting older people in Minsk in a professional and person-centered way.Specifically this project aims to improve the quality of life of older people in Minsk who are mainly isolated without family support. The project will support those caring for a relative with dementia and increase awareness of dementia to create a more tolerant community. Befriending services (by volunteers) will be provided to isolated people approximately twice a month.From October 2025 to March 2026, this project will reach around 75 people with regular dementia support and befriending services, and over 100 people through trainings and individual consultations. Dementia support will vary person to person, but focusing on activities to stimulate memory, prevent cognitive decline, and maintain communication skills. Depending on the beneficiaries&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; physical and cognitive state, activities will take place at home, at a day centre, or online. Staff will deliver training on person-centred care and practical aspects of caring for people with dementia. They will support other organisations that serve the Belarusian Jewish community by sharing knowledge and best practice.</narrative>
  </description>
